  "notes": "The Sabatini hospital frames a rectangular garden with an ashlar base, ordered limestone and lime plaster bays, and a dark roof. Twin glazed public lifts and the rear service lift contrast with the historic walls. Three Nouvel volumes form a public court under a tapered red canopy with nineteen daylight openings. The four PMTiles polygons and standard Terrarium terrain fix the exterior plan and signed orientation. Cornice, bridge and canopy elevations, panel rhythms and the garden planting are exterior photo estimates. The Sabatini garden and Nouvel court remain open. Gallery interiors, collection artworks, changing signage and exhibition furniture are outside the exterior scope.",
